  "build": {
    "buildCommand": "git add -A && git commit -q -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nprompts: state the bare-machine prerequisites, and guard skimmability directly\n\nA fresh agent was told to run git and npm without ever being told it needed\nthem. The requestor prompt now opens with an explicitly skippable list of what\na bare machine requires: git, Node 22+, the five hosts it must reach, and\npermission to leave a command running. Worth saying plainly that the dependency\nsurface is one package, viem, and nothing global.\n\nThe line cap went 40, then 60, and would now go to 75 -- a number I keep\nraising is a number that was never measuring the right thing. What it defended\nagainst was a wall of text nobody reads to the end, so that is asserted\ndirectly now: no unbroken run over 12 lines, and headings must exist. The cap\nstays as a backstop.\n\nThat new check immediately failed payer.md, which had no headings at all. It\nhas them now -- and its staged narration sentences are gone too, replaced with\n\"describe what is on the screen\". Those were the same scripted lines a cautious\nagent objected to in the requestor prompt; the objection did not stop being\nvalid because this side runs on our own machine.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\n)\" && git branch -f claude/handshake-v6 main && git push -q origin main && git push -q --force-with-lease origin claude/handshake-v6 && echo \"handshake pushed\"; R=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-Kailor-Documents-Projects-handshake/07afa53e-82b5-48a5-81cf-db1b435412ba/scratchpad/research; cd \"$R\" && npm run build 2>&1 | grep -E \"error|Compiled successfully\" | head -2 && git add -A && git commit -q -m \"handshake/claude-v6: publish the prompts with bare-machine prerequisites\" && (git push -q origin main 2>/dev/null || (git pull --rebase -q origin main && git push -q origin main)) && echo \"site pushed\"",
    "testCommand": "wc -l prompts/requestor.md && npm test 2>&1 | grep -E \"^# (tests|pass|fail)|^not ok\" | head -4; echo; echo \"=== page: does it repeat the 'no account' claim? ===\"; R=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-Kailor-Documents-Projects-handshake/07afa53e-82b5-48a5-81cf-db1b435412ba/scratchpad/research; grep -n \"no account\\|no key, no password\" \"$R/src/components/ClaudeV6Runbook.tsx\" | head -3",
